pwm1:m:ProofOfWork.Me WORK Pricing Protocol V2

Effective from the activation point named by this declaration, a WORK marketplace listing, seal, or purchase is valid only when its total seller price is greater than or equal to the canonical WORK network-value floor.

For an action confirmed at block H:

minimumPriceSats =
ceil(
  amountAtoms * liveNetworkValueSats(H-1)
  / (21000000 * workAtomsPerWork)
)

liveNetworkValueSats(H-1) must come from the last green canonical ProofOfWork Computer ledger snapshot, bound to the exact hash of block H-1.

Every V2 listing, seal, and purchase must identify the oracle block height, oracle block hash, network value, amountAtoms, and minimum price used for validation.

A missing, stale, hash-mismatched, inconsistent, or below-floor action is invalid and causes no canonical WORK balance, ownership, marketplace, sale, Log, Growth, or network-value mutation.

Only transactions accepted by these deterministic rules are canonical ProofOfWork Computer WORK actions. Third-party and OTC transfers are not canonical WORK state transitions unless they satisfy the active protocol and are accepted by the canonical verifier.

Confirmed chain history is authoritative. Pending transactions provide visibility only.